# SC8180X / Xiaomi Book S 12.4: corrected SSC accelerometer mount matrix.
#
# Facts that pin this down (per the BIOS/native image direction, corroborated
# by the DRM mode): the panel's native mode is 1600x2560, i.e. PORTRAIT, so a
# keyboard-attached landscape desktop needs mutter to apply a 90/270 degree
# transform (1 or 3).
#
# iio-sensor-proxy's orientation.c classifies the (already quirked) vector as:
#     portrait_rotation  = atan2(x, sqrt(y*y + z*z))
#     landscape_rotation = atan2(y, sqrt(x*x + z*z))
# |portrait| > 35 deg picks left-up/right-up from the SIGN OF X; otherwise
# |landscape| > 35 deg picks bottom-up/normal from the SIGN OF Y.
# mutter maps normal -> 0, left-up -> 90 (1), bottom-up -> 180 (2),
# right-up -> 270 (3).  There is no transform 8.
#
# First attempt here was 0,-1,0;1,0,0;0,0,1.  It is wrong: it rotates the raw
# frame by 90 deg, so the keyboard-landscape hold lands in the LANDSCAPE branch
# and reports "bottom-up" -> transform 180, i.e. an upside-down portrait image.
# (The "transform 8" it was originally chosen for does not exist.)
#
# What the earlier matrix sweep left installed in /etc was
# 1,0,0;0,-1,0;0,0,1 - a REFLECTION (det = -1), not a rotation.  It inverts the
# handedness of the sensor frame, so the two portrait holds read correctly while
# the two landscape holds are swapped: observed on hardware as "portrait fine,
# both landscape holds 180 deg out".
#
# The fix is the 180 degree rotation about the screen normal below (det = +1):
#     -1,  0, 0     display x = -raw x   (swaps left-up <-> right-up)
#      0, -1, 0     display y = -raw y   (keeps normal <-> bottom-up)
#      0,  0, 1     display z =  raw z   (screen normal)
# Checked against the 18 (quirked vector -> orientation) pairs logged while
# rotating the device: all 8 portrait samples keep their label, all 10
# landscape samples swap.
#
# libssc applies the vendor matrix to every sample before iio-sensor-proxy sees
# it, so this cannot be corrected through the sensor properties - hence the
# ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX override in drv-ssc-accel.c, the same property the IIO
# drivers already honour.
SUBSYSTEM=="misc", KERNEL=="fastrpc-sdsp*", ENV{ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX}="-1,0,0;0,-1,0;0,0,1"
